docs {
  # Update Attachment Metadata (Protected)

  **Method:** `PATCH`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/attachments/:id`
  **Auth:** Required (Bearer Token)

  ## Description

  Updates editable metadata of an existing attachment (e.g. original filename, group association, expense association, type, and public access flag). Enforces ownership verification so only the uploader can edit the record.

  ## Request

  ### Headers

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Yes | Bearer access token (`Bearer <token>`) |
  | `Content-Type` | `string` | Yes | `application/json` |

  ### Body

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `original_filename` | `string` | No | New original filename |
  | `group_id` | `int64` | No | Associated squad/group ID |
  | `expense_id` | `int64` | No | Associated expense ID |
  | `type` | `string` | No | New attachment type |
  | `is_public` | `boolean` | No | Public flag |

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`**
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 1,
      "original_filename": "updated_avatar_name.png",
      "is_public": true
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  * `401 Unauthorized` — Missing or invalid token
  * `403 Forbidden` — User is not the owner of the attachment
  * `404 Not Found` — Attachment does not exist
}
